Number 1 Dip/Spread in the world: Toum! 
. 
Im on a mission to recreate the world’s best sauces. We’re starting with what was just ranked as number one on the list: Toum. 
 
Its a garlicky spread that is out of this world good on any kind of protein, veggie, or by the spoonful 😅💥 
. 
Ingredients: 
✅1/2 cup peeled fresh garlic cloves 
✅Juice of 1 lemon (approximately 2 tablespoons) 
✅2 pinches of salt 
✅1 cup avocado oil (or a neutral oil) 
 
Here is how to make it: 
 
1.Grab a medium mason jar, just wide enough to fit an immersion blender. 
. 
2. Place 1/2 cup of peeled garlic cloves at the bottom of the mason jar. Add the juice of 1 lemon (Approx 2 TBSP) and 2 pinches salt. 
. 
3. Use the immersion blender to blend the mixture into a smooth garlic paste. Make sure there no chunks, and the consistency is smooth! 
. 
4.Pour 1 cup of avocado oil (or a neutral oil) into the jar with the garlic paste. 
. 
5.Insert the immersion blender all the way to the bottom of the mason jar and blend without moving the blender up and down. Keep it at the base of the jar and blend slowly, bringing it up just a little every minute until you reach the top. This process should take about 5 minutes. Be patient; it’s worth it! 
. 
6.Spoon the toum spread onto a plate to serve, or use it to elevate any kind of protein (chicken, steak, fish), or veggie. You can store by by putting a lid on the jar and keep in the fridge for 1-2 weeks. 